REGRESSION FINDING (pre-existing, NOT introduced by this diff — profile_screen.dart
is not one of the 4 files touched by NEARS-2751 and was not modified by this
change). Filed as a regression_bug per QA process, non-blocking for this
ticket.

profile_screen.dart body:
  return (isLoggedIn && profileController.userInfoModel == null)
      ? const Center(child: CircularProgressIndicator())
      : Stack(...)   // the static menu incl. "My Address" only renders here

i.e. the ENTIRE Profile tab (including the static "My Address" menu entry)
is gated behind a successful GET /api/v1/customer/info. When that endpoint
is down, Profile never renders anything but a bare, unlabeled spinner — with
no error/retry affordance (the exact "infinite spinner" class of bug NEARS-2751
just fixed for address_screen.dart, but not yet applied to profile_screen.dart).

Live log evidence (repeated retries, ~30s apart, never resolving to an error
state or a degraded render):

09-01 14:27:30.141 30734 30734 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/info http_status=null type=ApiFailure transport_error=timeout msg="api request threw" correlation_id=e09ce1ca-20b6-447f-8a69-ad6ce2cd12c0
09-01 14:27:30.142 30734 30734 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/info http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="profile load failed"
09-01 14:27:58.569 30734 30734 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/info http_status=null type=ApiFailure transport_error=timeout msg="api request threw" correlation_id=429c0cc3-3065-4579-8d73-18b65825f61a
09-01 14:27:58.572 30734 30734 I flutter : [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/customer/info http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="profile load failed"

Live-observed effect: polled the Profile tab every 5s for 55s straight during
the outage; labelled-node count stayed at 0 (bare spinner) for all but two
5s windows, where a transient unstyled "Timed out. Please try again after few
minutes" line appeared then reverted to the spinner. "My Address" never became
reachable during the whole window.

Practical consequence for THIS ticket's QA: Profile -> My Address is the ONLY
documented/reachable navigation entry to address_screen.dart (confirmed via
grep across lib/ for RouteHelper.address / AddressScreen( callers — none
found outside route_helper.dart's own GetPage registration and
profile_screen.dart's menu tap). A full backend outage therefore blocks
reaching the AC4 target screen via normal UI navigation, which is why AC4's
live evidence for NEARS-2751 is the real [FAIL] log capture on the address/list
endpoint + a live-executed passing widget test, rather than a full on-screen
screenshot of the NErrorRetry card. Suggest tracking profile_screen.dart's own
infinite-spinner gap as a follow-up ticket (same NEARS-2013/NEARS-2751 pattern,
different screen).
